course: dictionary
lesson: 11942
title: Canvassing: asking for support
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Canvassing means going from house to house, or talking to people, to ask for their votes or support. It is most often linked to an election, when people choose a leader or a party. «Maya spent Saturday canvassing for the school council candidate.» Here canvassing means knocking on doors and asking people to vote for her.
explain: Canvassing can also mean asking many people for their opinions. «The school canvassed parents' views with a short survey.» Clue words such as votes, support, election, opinions and survey tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. Ask: who is doing the asking, and who are they asking? If the answer is voters or people, the meaning is about votes or support. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Canvassing means asking people for their votes, their support, or their opinions.
fact: «Canvassing» is the -ing form of the verb canvass, and it can also be a noun for the activity as a whole, as in «canvassing for votes».
fact: Common phrases include «go canvassing», «canvassing for votes» and «canvassing opinions».
fact: Canvass can also mean discussing an idea in detail, but this meaning is less common.
fact: Canvassing is often done before an election, when candidates and their helpers knock on doors and hand out leaflets.
exercise: «Maya spent Saturday canvassing for the school council candidate.» What is canvassing here? | Painting a picture on a large cloth | Cleaning the classroom windows | Running a race around the park | *Going door to door asking people for their votes
exercise: «The school canvassed parents' views with a short survey.» What does canvassed mean here? | Ignored everyone's ideas completely | Sang a song for the parents | *Asked many people for their opinions | Lost the survey forms
exercise: «Before the election, the team went canvassing in the village.» Which word in this sentence tells you canvassing is linked to voting? | team | village | went | *election
test: Ravi knocks on every door on the street, asking people to support his plan. What is Ravi doing? | Painting the fence | Delivering the post | *Canvassing | Gardening
test: What does «canvassing opinions» mean? | Hiding from people | Counting coins in a jar | *Asking people what they think | Losing a bet
exam: «The team spent the whole week canvassing views on the new park.» What is the best meaning of canvassing here? | Writing a poem | *Asking many people for their opinions | Sleeping late | Going cycling
